The probability that the fourth ball selected is black is equal to the proportion of black balls in the box, which is \( \frac{3}{6} = \frac{1}{2} \). This follows from symmetry, as each ball is equally likely to appear in any position in a random sequence.

Among the given options, both b and c are \( \frac{1}{2} \). Assuming a possible typo, the intended correct option is likely b.

\boxed{b}

The probability that a leap year has 53 Sundays is \(\frac{2}{7}\). This is because a leap year has 366 days, which consists of 52 complete weeks plus 2 extra days. The 52 weeks contribute 52 Sundays, and the extra days contribute an additional Sunday if they include Sunday. The extra days are consecutive, and there are 7 equally likely pairs of consecutive days corresponding to the starting day of the year. The favorable pairs are (Saturday, Sunday) and (Sunday, Monday), which occur when January 1 is Saturday or Sunday, respectively. Thus, 2 out of 7 possibilities yield 53 Sundays.

The correct option is **e) 2/7**.

\boxed{e}
